root — THE SCREEN.

The window with no parent. It composites itself by a convention (three
columns at large, the middle one splitting into two rows) and then forgets
they were ever special: nothing downstream can tell those columns from any
others, because there is no pane type and no reserved name.

Its type-specific verb is Reset, because it is the only window with a
default to return to. An arbitrary column has no canonical arrangement, so
Reset there would either mean nothing or mean Fit.
